8. ACCESSIBILITY, LOW BANDWIDTH, VOICE
=====================================================
- Touch targets >= 48px; visible 3px focus ring; contrast AA or better; works at 200% zoom; every control has a Telugu accessible name; results announced via aria-live; full keyboard use; lang="te" on Telugu text.
- Every verdict and every checklist row is readable aloud. Voice is a first-class path, not an add-on.
- Voice recording: check MediaRecorder support and mimeType (webm/opus vs mp4 on iOS Safari); handle permission denied, no mic, and interruptions with clear Telugu messages. Max 60 seconds with a visible countdown. If server ASR needs WAV, encode 16 kHz 16-bit mono WAV in the browser (decodeAudioData + OfflineAudioContext). Fall back to Web Speech API (te-IN), then to text input.
- TTS: if no audio provider works, hide the Listen button gracefully and show a one-line Telugu note. Do not leave a dead button.
- Share card: draw it on a canvas at 1080x1350. Wait for document.fonts.load for the Telugu fonts before drawing (otherwise the card renders in a fallback font). Share via navigator.share({files}) when canShare returns true; otherwise download the PNG and offer a wa.me text link.
- Budgets (mid-range Android, Slow 4G): LCP <= 2.5s; initial JS <= 150 KB gzip on /; no raster images; fonts subset and preloaded. Lighthouse mobile: Performance >= 85, Accessibility >= 95, Best Practices >= 95, SEO >= 90.
- Service worker: hand-written, versioned cache, cache-first for static assets, network-first for /api, an offline page. Register in production only, with a safe update path.

=====================================================
9. SECURITY AND PRIVACY
=====================================================
- Validate every input with zod: text <= 4000 chars, URL <= 2048, audio <= 60s and 2 MB, image <= 5 MB. Rate limit all API routes by hashed IP with a daily salt (never store raw IPs).
- Never store raw messages, screenshots or audio. Radar stores only: registrable domain, verdict, scheme id, action type, district, hour bucket.
- Radar submission is opt-in with a plain-language Telugu explanation. No personal data, ever.
- Never use dangerouslySetInnerHTML. CSP with nonces, HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, Referrer-Policy: no-referrer, Permissions-Policy allowing microphone for self only.
- No third-party analytics, trackers or CDNs. Never log raw user input. Errors returned to clients are generic.
- Admin: password from env compared in constant time, httpOnly sameSite cookie, rate-limited, audit log of changes. Publishing a registry entry requires sourceUrl and verifiedOn.
- npm audit must show no high or critical issues.

